<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26219" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēnīmen</span></b> ,
		ĭnis, n.
		lenio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a softening</i> or <i>soothing remedy; an
				alleviation, mitigation, solace</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">testudo laborum Dulce lenimen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 32, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollicitae lenimen dulce senectae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 500</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">addidit illis hoc quoque lenimen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 11, 450</span></i>
			.</div>
